# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EmailJS — contact form delivery
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own values:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. This file (.env.example) is committed and must
# NEVER contain real values — it only documents which keys are required.
#
# Find these in your EmailJS dashboard (https://dashboard.emailjs.com):
#   Public Key  → Account → General → Public Key
#   Service ID  → Email Services → your service
#   Template ID → Email Templates → your template
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser. Everything
# here IS shipped to the client and is publicly readable — that is EmailJS's
# intended client-side model, so only ever put EmailJS's *public* key here.
# Never add an SMTP password, private API key or server secret to this file.
#
# Lock the key down in the EmailJS dashboard (see Account → Security):
#   • restrict it to your production domain
#   • keep the rate limit enabled
# Without that, anyone can lift the key from your bundle and send through
# your template.
#
# After changing any value, restart the dev server — Vite reads .env at boot.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
